  speakerName: Aling Rosa
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Aww, thank you!

    When you look at something or notice something
    with your eyes, the Ilokano verb ''makita'' means ''see.''

    For example,
    you can use it when looking at these bright textiles.

    Listen carefully:
    makita.

    Now, try saying ''makita'' yourself.'
